      "problem": "The cube of every rational number is rational.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"every\" indicates we should use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to rational numbers. So, by denoting a rational number as $x,$ we have that \n\n$$\n∀\\,x\\in Q.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as \n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\in Q.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows: \n\n$∀\\,x\\in Q,\\,{x}^{3}\\in Q.$",
